# The interpretation. Never committed, on any branch, for any reason — the
# whole experiment is only meaningful while the discovery side of the tree has
# no access to it. tools/leakguard.py enforces the same boundary in the working
# copy; this enforces it in history.
secret/

# Environment and build output
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
theory/.lake/

# Generated Lean. `Anonymous.lean` and `spec.json` are committed deliberately —
# they are produced by the generator inside secret/, so without them a clone
# would have no theory to run against at all.
theory/Theory/B[0-9]*.lean
theory/Theory/Concepts.lean

# The handoff plan. Deliberately not committed: it is a working document for a
# fresh agent, superseded on every sprint. It lives under docs/ rather than at
# the root so tools/leakguard.py actually scans it.
docs/HANDOFF.md

# Run artifacts. Large, reproducible, and regenerated by every run:
#   uv run python -m pipeline.chainer.run --run-id main
#   uv run python -m pipeline.kernel.recheck --run main   (restores the two below)
runs/
generated/
metadata/

# The write-up. Gitignored, but still scanned by tools/leakguard.py -- the body
# is written in the anonymized vocabulary on purpose, so that every claim has to
# stand structurally. The interpretation belongs in an appendix outside this
# directory, never in here.
tex/
